{"step_index":309,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T18:40:12Z","input_tokens":3238,"cache_read_tokens":130251,"output_tokens":939,"thinking":"Extracted records from the system yielded 1167 entries in a very short time, indicating potential efficiency. The extracted data includes entries related to an account service, security service, and analytics platform, all timestamped and linked to the same evidence. The differing \"presence\" statuses across these entries warrant further investigation to understand their interdependencies.\n\n\nThe \"ANONYMIZED\" status for `export_001` appears incorrect; the presence of \"owner_email\" suggests identification. The current logic incorrectly treats missing \"email\" as a signal for anonymization when other identifying fields might be present.  The code must be updated to explicitly check for the absence of `user_id`, `email`, `phone`, and `email_hash`, and the presence of `eml` or `uid` to determine \"PRESENT\" status.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"BypassSandbox":true,"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nuid = None\neml = 'gabriel.costa@proton.me'\nitem = {'resource_id': 'export_001', 'owner_email': eml}\nif not uid and not eml and not item.get('phone') and not item.get('email_hash'):\n    state = 'ANONYMIZED'\nelse:\n    state = 'PRESENT'\nprint('State:', state)\n\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Test export_001 state logic"}}]}
